//! **Generated** by `_scratch/2026-09-29-carts/_make_palettes_rs.py` from gambatte's
//! `libgambatte/libretro/gbcpalettes.h` — do not edit by hand. The numbers, the names and the
//! order are the core's own; the only things this file does to them are drop the `PixelShift ` /
//! `TWB64 ` prefix (folded into a two-letter tag) and drop the entries that are not four
//! different colours, so a name seen on the device can be found in that header without a
//! translation table in between. The generator prints what it dropped.
//!
//! Two rules from that header are load-bearing and neither is obvious, so they are repeated
//! here: a `PACK15_4` literal is a plain `0xRRGGBB` (**not** the GBC's BGR555 word order), and
//! its four entries run **lightest first** — game colour 0 is the paper, index 3 the ink.
//! `GB_SHADE_LEVELS` is written the same way round, so this table needs no reordering.
//!
//! A palette is not required to climb in luminance: `Pip-Boy` and `Tron` put their background
//! last on purpose, which is what an inverted-looking scheme is. Nothing here assumes monotonic.
//!
